    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm stuck on my lit review. if i have a source with like 5 authors, how do i do the in-text citation for APA 7th? i also need to know how it's different if im using Chicago style. thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For APA 7th edition, when citing a source with five authors in the text, you list the first author followed by \"et al.\" from the very first citation onward. In contrast, Chicago style, depending on whether you use Notes-Bibliography or Author-Date, typically requires listing all authors in the bibliography. If you are using parenthetical citations in Chicago, you will usually include the author's last names and the year.",
