    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. so for chicago, if i'm using the notes-bibliography style, do i still use et al. in the footnote if there are 5 authors? or do i have to list all of them every single time? it seems like a lot of extra work to write them all out.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In Chicago Notes-Bibliography style, you should generally list all five authors in the *first* full footnote where you cite the source completely. For every subsequent citation to that same source, you can use a shortened form, often citing only the first author followed by \"et al.\" to save space. This allows you to avoid writing out all five names repeatedly throughout your notes.",
